{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_dilogarithm_evaluation","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L94-L103","doc":"**Exceptional-divisor summand = quantum dilogarithm**\n    ([`lem:topological-mass-dilogarithm`]).\n\n`‖MI∫_{E_i}‖ = Φ_q(z_i)` for every exceptional divisor `E_i`.\n*Derived* (not assumed): chain the chart evaluation with the proved\nintegral representation of `Φ_q`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:topological-mass-dilogarithm","label":"lem:topological-mass-dilogarithm","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-dilogarithm.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_divisor_chart_evaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.tm_divisor_chart_evaluation","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L83-L92","doc":"**Open analytic input — Briggs–Klein chart evaluation.**  In the\nspectral coordinates of the Briggs–Klein chart at `E_i`, the\nmultiplicative-integral norm evaluates to the q-dilogarithm\nintegral at `z_i`.  Needs Yekutieli multiplicative integration and\nthe Faddeev–Kashaev evaluation (neither in Mathlib). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs.chart_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs.chart_eval","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Open analytic input — Briggs–Klein chart evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.TmDivisorChartInputs","kind":"class","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L79-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.phi_q_integral_representation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.phi_q_integral_representation","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L74-L77","doc":"**Integral representation of `Φ_q`** — the .md's second equality,\nproved (definitionally) rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.Phi_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.Phi_q","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The Faddeev–Kashaev quantum dilogarithm, **defined** by its\nintegral representation `Φ_q(w) = ∫₀^{w} ln_q(1+t)/t dt` (the\n.md's second equality) as a Mathlib interval integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.z","kind":"opaque","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The Briggs–Klein spectral coordinate `z_i` at the exceptional\ndivisor `E_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.lnq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.lnq","kind":"opaque","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L59-L62","doc":"The q-logarithm `ln_q` (at the ambient deformation parameter `q`).\nIts q-series theory is not in Mathlib, so it stays opaque; the\ndilogarithm `Phi_q` below is a genuine integral of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MI","kind":"opaque","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_dilogarithm_evaluation.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The norm of the divisor-`i` non-abelian multiplicative integral\n`‖MI∫_{E_i}(∇_A q, L ∧ F⁺)‖`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}